All box access went through `tools/tb` (Ask-CK decision D6); no hand-built ssh line was used.

- `tools/tb precheck tb277 u2` · `tools/tb scratch tb277 cksnmpmon` · `tools/tb template tb277`
  · `tools/tb peek tb277 cksnmpmon u2 115200` · `tools/tb nics tb277`
- `tools/tb probe tb277 --consoles u2 --no-prompt --pdu 10.36.230.212 --outlet u2=1
  --name u2=swi_d --read-only --baud 115200` (before and after)
- `tools/tb ckcon tb277 cksnmpmon u2 115200 "<show command>" ...` -- the read-only captures
- `tools/tb cfg tb277 cksnmpmon u2 115200 "configure terminal" ... "end" ...` -- all config
- `tools/tb capture tb277 cksnmpmon eth3 <secs> <out>.pcap udp port 162` -- 60 s, 300 s, 150 s, 150 s
- `tools/tb tool tb277 cksnmpmon snmpwire /tmp/cksnmpmon/<file>.pcap --port 162 --values --abs`
- `tools/tb tool tb277 cksnmpmon snmpq get 10.38.22.34 <oid>... --v2c --community testing123`
- `tools/tb tool tb277 cksnmpmon ckcase AWPTCM-T33413`
- `python3 tools/rc2cfg.py` (the `.cfg`) and `python3 tools/rcdiff.py` (the teardown proof)
- 🆕 **`tools/tb awshell tb277 cksnmpmon u2 115200 --timeout <s> '<shell command>' ...`**

### The new tool: `tools/awshell.py`

Written for this run because **no existing tool could reach the device's shell**, and it is
generic, so it is in the repo-root `tools/` with a `tools/README.md` entry rather than in this
case's `work/` (logged-output.md §2). `awshell` was also added to the console-tool set in
`tools/tb`, so it is driven the same way as every other console tool.

Why the existing drivers could not do it: `console.PROMPT_RE` is
`[\w.-]+(?:\([\w -]+\))?#[ \t]*$`, which matches `awplus#` and `awplus(config)#` and **cannot
match `[root@awplus flash]#`** -- the character before the `#` is `]`. Every shell command sent
through `ckcon` or `cfg` would therefore run to its full timeout and the driver would then
abandon the rest of the batch (the same silent-truncation family as `console.ADVISORY` and the
prompt-splice bug already recorded in `tools/README.md`). `awshell.py` completes a command on
the shell's own `]#`/`]$` prompt instead, and **always returns the console to the AW+ exec
prompt**, reporting exit 5 if it cannot -- because a console left in a root shell is the
documented trap that makes the next run's `show` commands answer `ash: show: not found`.
It ran five times in this case and returned `awplus#` every time.

